Z||000008||artherd||12-14-2001||11:09 PM||||Rain?!?  You let a little sprinkle stop you?!?! Snow/salt is another story, bur RAIN!?<P>Rain is good, cleans out caked on dirt/dust! :P<P>I even drive the 70k mile T-top in the rain, of course, I wash her down after every trip.... (and not in downpours/traffic/bad-rain-stuff)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by California Kid:<BR><B>Just a lot of rain here in Michigan, but it spoiled my idea (as well as theirs) of meeting up with some of the Corvette Forum guys today. They had planned a final season "Cruise In" for this afternoon.<P>Looks like I'll just have to pop open the garage door, start her up, and listen to a couple tunes. Neighbors must think I'm nuts!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
